> On the productionisation side, three things I'd call out. Guardrails were layered: input and output filtering using both deterministic regex checks and LLM-as-a-judge, with the deterministic layer first because it's cheap, fast, and auditable, and the model-graded layer for the nuanced cases regex can't express. We also tuned the safety guardrails Vertex AI provides natively, the harm-category thresholds, rather than rebuilding what the platform gave us. Observability was OpenTelemetry across the retrieval path, traces, latency, and failure rates, so when quality dropped we could see which stage was responsible rather than guessing. And evaluation meant measuring retrieval separately from generation, because most 'the LLM is wrong' complaints are actually retrieval failures, and you can only fix what you can isolate.
