> The thing I care about most, and what I took from it, is the gap between an AI demo and a production AI system. Getting a demo working is easy. The engineering is in retrieval quality, evaluation, guardrails, and observability, treating the AI layer with the same testing and operational rigour as any production system. That's the same TDD-and-observability discipline I've run across banking and asset management, applied to AI."

**Fill with real texture before Friday (Tom will drill for these; have true specifics ready, and if a number does not exist say so rather than inventing one):**
- One concrete example of a query or content case the regex layer caught vs one the LLM-judge layer caught.
- Why Vertex/Gemini (what the decision actually turned on: platform alignment, data residency, model quality at the time).
